class Solution {
    public int countGoodSubstrings(String s) {

        HashSet<Character> set = new HashSet<>();

        int left = 0;
        int count = 0;

        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {

            // If duplicate comes, shrink the window
            while (set.contains(s.charAt(right))) {
                set.remove(s.charAt(left));
                left++;
            }

            // Add current character
            set.add(s.charAt(right));

            // Count all good substrings ending at right
            count += right - left + 1;
        }

        return count;
    }
}

/*
What is a “good substring”?

A substring is called good if it has no repeated characters.

For example:

s = "abc"

Substrings include:

"a"    → good ✅
"b"    → good ✅
"c"    → good ✅
"ab"   → good ✅
"bc"   → good ✅
"abc"  → good ✅

All characters are different.

So there are 6 good substrings. */
